0..74 Comment "// Implicit parameters: the telescope `[a : Type]` binds parameters of the"
75..154 Comment "// function. A use supplies them in the instantiation slot. It supplies them by"
155..230 Comment "// position in the written order, `same[Integer] 3`. Or it supplies them by"
231..276 Comment "// name in any order, `same[.a = Integer] 3`."
277..279 Comment "//"
280..312 Comment "// The implicit and the explicit"
313..388 Comment "// parameters merge into one telescope, each after every parameter its type"
389..461 Comment "// names, ties kept in the written order; which ones are implicit is the"
462..541 Comment "// declaration\'s metadata, so the declared type is the one the function written"
542..619 Comment "// with every parameter explicit, in the merged order, has. A call that omits"
620..694 Comment "// its implicits has each one solved from its arguments and the type it is"
695..774 Comment "// checked against. The checker solves a call in a declared type where the type"
775..784 Comment "// forms."
785..861 Comment "// What refuses is in `../pathological/classifier/implicit-telescope.gandr`."
862..864 Comment "//"
865..879 Comment "// - see: #315"
880..895 Comment "// - see: #1216"
896..928 Comment "// - see: #1498 — `identityAt`"
929..959 Comment "// - see: #1188 — `twiceRun`"
960..992 Comment "// - see: #5026 — `sameSigned`"
